    "headline": "Travis County Home Backup Report",
    "summary": "Homes in Travis County face an elevated risk. A long outage of 12 hours or more happens about once every 10 years based on 8 years of records since 2018. In February 2021, 43% of homes in the county lost power. The longest-waiting tenth waited about 96 hours. In February 2023, 29% of homes in the county lost power. The longest-waiting tenth waited about 132 hours. One Core lasts about 18 hours in August. One Core lasts about 44 hours in February. Two Cores are suggested. Two Cores cover 89% of past 12-hour-plus outage hours. Base confirms sizing at install.",
